    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d412">

                <pb facs="0454" n="370" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. No. 614.119/103</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Guatemala</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Leavell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-18T17:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 18, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your September 12, 3 p.m. You may inform Guatemala Government that when its Alien
                    Property Custodian is given full authority to sell the German property, the War
                    Trade Board will be pleased to license freely supplies for Empresa Electrica de
                    Guatemala.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
